-- Fix public model descriptions that describe the wrong kind of model or were
-- copied from another model (2026-11-04 catalogue audit, all ~1,782 public rows read).
--
-- Problems fixed here (388 rows; wrong_type 178, copied 107, placeholder 38, video_template 31, wrong_family 18, empty 11, wrong_vendor 3, moe 2):
-- * A templated generator confused video input with video generation: text
--   models (Gemma 3/4, Amazon Nova, Kimi K2.5, Qwen VL, GLM 5V ...) said they turn
--   still images into animated clips, and some were called video generation models.
-- * Other templates gave the wrong model type: Google models called text-to-speech
--   "a substantial generational step up from Gemini 2.5 Flash TTS", ElevenLabs,
--   MiniMax and StepFun speech models called chat language models, embedding and
--   search models called web search or chat models, TranslateGemma called an image
--   generator, Grok 0-2 called text-to-speech.
-- * Text pasted from a different model (GLM-5.1 text on GLM-4 rows, Qwen3 text on
--   Qwen2.5, Nemotron Super text on OpenReasoning, Llama 3.3 text on Llama 4, ...),
--   wrong family claims (FLUX.1 called FLUX.2, Qwen3 called Qwen3-Next, Gemma 3
--   called Mixture-of-Experts), and empty or placeholder text.
-- New text uses the model's catalogue metadata and vendor documentation; facts
-- that could not be confirmed (context sizes, parameter counts) were left out.

-- Guarded on the description observed during the 2026-11-04 audit: each row
-- carries the first 12 hex characters of md5(description) as it was then (null
-- for an empty description), so a row edited since is left alone. Row-level
-- history, including the previous text, is recorded by the catalogue_row_history
-- trigger on public.v2_models.
with fixes (model_slug, old_description_md5, new_description) as (
values
